{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/600407-battling-it-out-statistics-style","id":600407,"title":"Battling it out, statistics style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-23T05:38:33-07:00","id":600407,"title":"Battling it out, statistics style","content":"Ironically, I much prefer the style of roleplay that doesn't make use of dice, and focuses much more on story than on stats.<br /> <br /> However, I also like to program and rank things ^_^<br /> <br /> I previously did a series comparing vampires and werewolves in physical combat. But there were a few flaws - I didn't include grappling, and the werewolves followed simplistic decisions. So I'll be doing a second series solving those issues. And it will be more general - I'll be including the top Vampire, Kuei-Jin, Werewolf (undecided on the other Fera), Wraith, Risen, Hunter, Demon, Mummy, Changeling, Ghoul, Human, and maybe Mage.<br /> <br /> The rules are:<br /> 1) All the characters must be legal starting characters for the system.<br /> 2) It is purely physical combat.<br /> 3) Combat happens in the physical world (so Wraiths must Embody).<br /> 4) Each character has the choice of their own natural abilities, or a Strength+2 sword.<br /> 5) Each character gets one pre-combat turn to prepare, unless there's a compelling reason to allow them more.<br /> 6) Side bets are allowed and encouraged.<br /> <br /> So my general question is what people think is the best possible fighter in each category. My specific question on this subforum is whether any one can come up with a better combat werewolf than: Get_of_Fenris_ultra_Metis Strength 2 Dexterity 6 Stamina 3 Wits 5 Brawl 5 Athletics 5 Willpower 4 Rage 10 Razor_claws Visage_of_Fenris.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 07-23-2015, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T03:50:06-07:00","id":601560,"title":"","content":"Where does the Dex 6 come from?<br /> <br /> Additionally, if it doesn't come from the choice of a totem, how about taking one, as well as possibly some interesting fetish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T14:17:13-07:00","id":602257,"title":"","content":"With all respect granted to the pure dice combat nature of this thought experiment--I have my doubts that a Rage 10 Metis will live long enough to get to these skill levels!<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can throw some critters into the pot, here. It'll be an excuse to start looking at Mokele for once. It'll also be fun to see what I can pull off with Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T23:09:32-07:00","id":602607,"title":"","content":"Changelings might be oddly complicated, what with Dragon's Ire. That ability along can change entire battles.<br /> <br /> I've had a Changeling player, playing an enraged 19 year old girl (Sidhe) take a solid (Rage boosted) hit from a Crinos Gurahl and take 0 damage. The Gurahl player's reaction was hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T04:03:27-07:00","id":605448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/600407-battling-it-out-statistics-style?p=601560#post601560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does the Dex 6 come from?<br /> <br /> Additionally, if it doesn't come from the choice of a totem, how about taking one, as well as possibly some interesting fetish?</div> </div> </div> </div>It indeed came from a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T04:14:51-07:00","id":605451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/600407-battling-it-out-statistics-style?p=602257#post602257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all respect granted to the pure dice combat nature of this thought experiment--I have my doubts that a Rage 10 Metis will live long enough to get to these skill levels!</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we aren't bound by reasonableness or coherence, there's been a Malkavian with dementation following it around and sucking away all its rage, keeping it calm and upper class.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/600407-battling-it-out-statistics-style?p=602257#post602257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll see if I can throw some critters into the pot, here. It'll be an excuse to start looking at Mokele for once. It'll also be fun to see what I can pull off with Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, thanks! ^_^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T08:44:58-07:00","id":605622,"title":"","content":"&quot;I am fire... I am DEATH!&quot;<br /> <br /> Smaug (Mokole-mbembe)<br /> Unktehi Suchid Crowned Sun (annular eclipse; Unity-Crowned)<br /> <br /> Strength 3 (7/2), Dexterity 4 (3/4), Stamina 3 (12/4)<br /> Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 2<br /> Perception 2, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> <br /> Athletics 2, Alertness 3, Brawl 3, Expression 3, Primal-Urge 2<br /> Animal Ken 1, Stealth 2, Survival 2<br /> Enigmas 3, Occult 3, Rituals 3<br /> <br /> Backgrounds: Totem 5 (Dragon)<br /> <br /> Gifts: Heightened Senses, Speed of Thought; Totem grants Dragon's Breath<br /> <br /> Rage 6, Gnosis 10, Willpower 7<br /> <br /> Archid Traits: Armored Scales (x2), Behemoth (x4), Long Teeth, Tall (x1), Terrible Claws, Wings<br /> <br /> Attacks (Archid):<br /> Claw (6 dice to attack, difficulty 6, 10A base damage)<br /> Bite (6 dice to attack, difficulty 5, 10A base damage)<br /> Tackle (6 dice to attack, difficulty 7, 15L base damage)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T09:28:06-07:00","id":605650,"title":"","content":"Dragon's Breath was based of Rage, right? And God, that guy looks scary.<br /> The only question is... does he fit in the White Room? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would have gone for more Brawl, just to ensure a more reliable hit ratio, but I assume his soak willl let him live long enough to murder everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 07-28-2015, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T09:37:02-07:00","id":605653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/600407-battling-it-out-statistics-style?p=605650#post605650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon's Breath was based of Rage, right? And God, that guy looks scary.<br /> The only question is... does he fit in the White Room? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You spend Rage points, one per two levels (only the first, you can spend more if you hit). Who knows if it keeps the soak difficulty from when it was originally written (9, as a chemical fire)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would have gone for more Brawl, just to ensure a more reliable hit ratio, but I assume his soak willl let him live long enough to murder everything. </div> </div> </div>Quite frankly, I'm not even being serious about this. The Traits that make Mokole huge don't even have entirely sensible rules attached to them, and no one ever thought to consider the possibility of using wing buffets to produce high-speed winds, Long Teeth and Terrible Claws are and always have been kind of weaksauce, too. I just wanted to stat out an Archid form that was based off of Smaug, so that I would stop idly thinking about it all the time. A more sensible combatant would probably be high Dex and Brawl with Typhon as a Totem, another auspice, and perhaps smaller and with way more armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:55:59-07:00","id":613984,"title":"","content":"Don't know the system all that well, but I recall a build my friends called &quot;Death Factory.&quot;<br /> <br /> I believe it was a Mokole with Giant Size and Poison Spikes, and it's only tactic was &quot;Fall down on thing, spend a Rage to roll over.&quot; <br /> <br /> That said I have no idea if it's actually effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:31:20-07:00","id":616055,"title":"","content":"It's effectiveness is entirely dependant on how the storyteller actually interprets Giant Size working in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}